WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.990 --> 00:00:06.900
So obviously it's best for all of us if this goes as smoothly as possible. Less stress, that's the operative word here.

00:00:11.610 --> 00:00:14.300
I've said that you can't just pop by--Just five minutes

00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:15.840
Can I borrow your warm hat?

00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:18.020
You said hey to Auntie Beth?

00:00:18.020 --> 00:00:23.149
My son, my sister, and her husband took care of him while I was in prison and now they won't share custody.

00:00:23.699 --> 00:00:27.829
It's not my clients, who are going to hear the word manslaughter attached to their name.

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:30.859
I was released on good behaviour a year ago.

00:00:31.380 --> 00:00:33.380
I gave you my phone number.

00:00:33.510 --> 00:00:35.280
Why? -Well argued.

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:38.380
What's with the ten year gap in the employment history?

00:00:38.380 --> 00:00:40.900
I really need this job, i'm trying to get my son back.

00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:44.540
It's really messed up, I'd be surprised if she ever sees that kid again.

00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:49.940
This girl I was representing didn't fit the picture of what a good person is supposed to look like.

00:00:51.700 --> 00:00:52.880
Neither do you.

00:00:54.570 --> 00:00:56.640
Do you want to get a drink?

00:00:56.640 --> 00:00:59.719
Pretty much all I do is drink with strangers, so... you'll do.

00:01:02.670 --> 00:01:04.670
It's like a different kind of nightmare.

00:01:05.549 --> 00:01:08.989
There's a monster out there and I can't see it and I can't fight it.

00:01:09.569 --> 00:01:11.500
See, what they're trying to do is trying to beat you.

00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:12.100
What is up with you?

00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:13.680
Come over here and say that to me again!

00:01:14.969 --> 00:01:15.600
It's understandable.

00:01:15.700 --> 00:01:17.000
It's not understandable they won't let me see my son.

00:01:18.020 --> 00:01:18.520
Well, no, I didn't--

00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:19.669
Don't ever touch me again, okay?

00:01:23.799 --> 00:01:29.039
Where does this go, in your mind, when you were planning this whole thing out, where is the best place that this goes?

00:01:30.799 --> 00:01:34.760
My spirit has had too many tests, I don't think it can take anymore.

00:01:34.780 --> 00:01:36.480
This is the part where you say, "Yes, your honor."

00:01:44.040 --> 00:01:46.200
Shut up-shut up!

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:51.680
Bad things happen to people who don't deserve it everyday and it's going to happen over and over again.

00:01:54.750 --> 00:01:59.069
I just need one person to take a chance on me.

